            <h3>Trend 1: The "De-Cored" Bank Core System Architecture</h3>
            <p>Financial technology experts are outlining a shift toward "de-=
cored" bank core systems driven by AI. Traditional centralized databases are =
being replaced by decentralized, componentized architectures that natively su=
pport AI agents and Web3.</p>
            <p>Under this model, core banking functions are broken down into =
"atomic blocks" exposed via standardized APIs. This allows AI agents to act a=
s the primary users, orchestrating transactions and managing digital assets s=
eamlessly.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">Transitioning to a de-cored architectu=
re allows banks to eliminate transaction bottlenecks and support real-time ri=
sk pricing. This structural flexibility is essential for integrating central =
bank digital currencies and tokenized real-world assets.</p>
            <p><a href=3D"http://stock.10jqka.com.cn/20260920/c680089352.shtm=
l">Read more</a></p>
           =20
            <h3>Trend 2: Transitioning from Cloud-Native to AI-Native Banking=
</h3>
            <p>ICBC and Huawei have co-released a white paper detailing the e=
volution of banking architectures from cloud-native to AI-native. This framew=
ork positions artificial intelligence as a core production factor rather than=
 an auxiliary tool.</p>
            <p>The white paper addresses the challenges of fragmented AI pilo=
ts by proposing unified agent engines and knowledge graphs. This ensures that=
 AI decisions remain highly accurate, reliable, and compliant with strict fin=
ancial regulations.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">Adopting an AI-native paradigm enables=
 banks to transition from simple automated workflows to deep human-machine co=
llaboration. This shift will dramatically improve operational efficiency whil=
e maintaining the stability and traceability of financial decisions.</p>
            <p><a href=3D"http://news.cnfol.com/shangyeyaowen/20260920/323757=
28.shtml">Read more</a></p>

            <h3>Trend 3: Innovative Credit Products: "Computing Power Loans"<=
/h3>
            <p>Banks in Shanghai are launching specialized financial products=
 like "Computing Power Loans" to support the growing AI industry. These produ=
cts shift the credit evaluation focus from physical collateral to technologic=
al assets and data.</p>
            <p>By assessing variables such as computing efficiency, core rese=
arch talent, and intellectual property, banks can extend credit to asset-ligh=
t AI startups. This addresses the high R&D costs and rapid technology iterati=
ons characteristic of the sector.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">This credit innovation represents a fu=
ndamental shift in commercial banking risk assessment. Shifting from "brick-a=
nd-mortar" collateral to digital and intellectual assets allows banks to capt=
ure high-growth market segments safely.</p>
            <p><a href=3D"http://field.10jqka.com.cn/20260920/c680087756.shtm=
l">Read more</a></p>

            <h3>Trend 4: Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) Redefining Bran=
d Visibility</h3>
            <p>As generative AI search engines gain massive adoption, traditi=
onal search engine optimization is transitioning to Generative Engine Optimiz=
ation. Brand visibility is no longer about keyword rankings but securing cita=
tions within AI-generated answers.</p>
            <p>AI engines prioritize highly authoritative, verifiable, and cr=
oss-referenced sources when generating responses. This has created a structur=
ed hierarchy of information sources, where official white papers and top-tier=
 media hold the highest weight.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">Financial institutions must adapt thei=
r marketing and public relations strategies to target AI indexing algorithms.=
 Failing to secure high-authority citations will result in a systematic loss =
of digital visibility and customer acquisition channels.</p>
            <p><a href=3D"http://www.wabei.cn/Home/News/364695">Read more</a>=
</p>

            <h3>Trend 5: AI-Enabled Remote Patient Monitoring and Decision Su=
pport</h3>
            <p>The remote patient monitoring sector is evolving rapidly throu=
gh the integration of AI-enabled decision support tools. Companies like DexCo=
m are connecting continuous glucose monitors directly to electronic health re=
cords and clinical portals.</p>
            <p>These platforms leverage machine learning algorithms to analyz=
e real-time patient data, predict health risks, and deliver actionable insigh=
ts to clinicians. This transition from passive data collection to active supp=
ort helps mitigate healthcare workforce shortages.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">For financial underwriters and health =
insurance providers, real-time AI health monitoring enables highly personaliz=
ed risk pricing. Access to continuous, verified health data allows insurers t=
o design dynamic premium structures and reduce overall claims.</p>
            <p><a href=3D"https://aktiensensor.com/articles/dexcom-leads-rpm-=
evolution-ai-interoperability--strong-reimbursement-for-cgm-success/">Read mo=
re</a></p>

